      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-317695",
      ":question/problem": "A manager has less than $$500$ to purchase coffee beans. To qualify for a wholesale discount, she must buy more than $100$ kilograms in total. Standard beans cost $$2.70$ per kilogram and premium beans cost $$8.50$ per kilogram. Rounded to one decimal place, what is the maximum weight of premium beans the manager can purchase while staying within the budget and keeping the discount?\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
