      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-318035",
      ":question/problem": "A supplies manager wants to spend more than $$500$ to purchase tea leaves. To qualify for a wholesale discount, she must buy at most $120$ kilograms in total. Standard green leaves cost $$2.90$ per kilogram and premium oolong leaves cost $$7.40$ per kilogram. Rounded to one decimal place, what is the minimum weight of premium oolong leaves the manager can purchase while staying within the budget cap on weight and exceeding the budget threshold on cost?\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
